OK.

Let's assume you've plonked the NetHack folder inside /Applications 
[change all path names that follow accordingly if you have it 
somewhere else...]

Open terminal.app

Type the following:

cd /Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/Contents/MacOS/
ln -fs /Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/nethackdir/ ./nethackdir


That will create a soft link to the nethackdir, and cause the chdir 
that was failing to work.

Now, if you login as the user wizard, open terminal and type:
/Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/Contents/MacOS/NetHack -D

It will work. [At least: it does for me.]

